  "2026-10-20T13:12:03.424Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR #174: fetched every review thread and all comments (one unresolved thread, PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s6uUtZt); latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Verified the shared csvImport handler returns success despite processImportRow recording create/update errors. Fix the shared result boundary and cover both CLI spellings, buffered/streamed imports and configured importers using real non-git trackers. The branch is current and includes main; dependency pins and gate thresholds stay unchanged."
  "2026-10-20T13:14:41.975Z",codex-agent,"The new public-host regression fails against the original shared handler: 0/1 passed, Missing expected rejection after two real mutation failures, while the command printed Imported 1, updated 1, skipped 4 (1 filtered out). The fix throws CommandError with exit code 1, counts and all row diagnostics before emitting a success receipt. Existing compensation/overrun tests now assert the nonzero command contract while retaining recovery and persisted-state checks. Whole-PR self-review found no separate handler instance: native, legacy, configured and streaming imports share this boundary; atomic failures already throw and dry-run performs no mutations."
  "2026-10-20T13:19:11.685Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for PRRT_kwDOSYpI8s6uUtZt: removed only the new res.errors guard from csvImport.run, leaving every test and the importer adapter unchanged. PATH with the pinned host plus node --test --test-name-pattern=\"reject partial\" test/commands.test.ts failed 0/1 (Missing expected rejection, exit 1). Restored the guard byte-for-byte afterward. Before the fix, node --test test/legacy-import-cli.test.ts also failed 0/1: expected process exit 1, received 0 with imported 1, updated 1, skipped 4 and two row errors. With the fix, the linked public-host test passed 1/1 across four buffered/streaming native/configured cases. The linked CLI test hit the default 120-second runner timeout under host load and is being retried with --timeout 600. No output containing scratch paths is persisted in this tracker."
